.TH CCHAN_ENABLE_SENDING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cchan_enable_sending \- turn on sends on a cchan direction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval cchan_enable_sending(cchan *ch, cchan_direction d);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Turns sends back on for one direction of the channel after
cchan_disable_sending() turned them off, and wakes every thread
that is blocked waiting to send.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to change
d    Direction that gets sends turned on (cchan_owner_to_workers or
     cchan_workers_to_owner)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - Sends are on again
ccol_invalid_args  - ch is NULL, or d is not valid
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Every blocked sender is woken with a broadcast, so a sender can try
again at once if the queue has free space. The other direction is left
as it is.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cchan_disable_sending (3)
